.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt DEVFS.CONF 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm devfs.conf
.Nd owners, modes and links for /dev
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr devfs 4
is made afresh at every boot, so owners, modes and links set in
.Pa /dev
by hand last only until reboot.
The
.Nm
file makes them permanent: the
.Pa /etc/rc.d/devfs
script applies it at boot, early, before
.Pa /etc/rc.d/tmp .
.Pp
Each line is an action, a device and an argument, separated by white
space.
Empty lines and lines starting with
.Ql #
are ignored.
The device is a name relative to
.Pa /dev ,
and for
.Cm own
and
.Cm perm
may be a shell pattern, which applies the action to every node it
matches.
.Bl -tag -width "perm dev mode"
.It Cm own Ar device Ar user Ns Op : Ns Ar group
Changes the owner, and the group if given, of the matching nodes, as
.Xr chown 8 .
.It Cm perm Ar device Ar mode
Changes the mode of the matching nodes to the octal
.Ar mode ,
as
.Xr chmod 1 .
.It Cm link Ar device Ar name
Creates
.Pa /dev/ Ns Ar name
as a symbolic link to
.Ar device ,
replacing whatever is there.
.Ar device
is not a pattern here.
.El
.Pp
A line with an unknown action, or naming a device that doesn't exist, is
skipped with a warning; the rest of the file still applies.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/rc.d/devfs -compact
.It Pa /etc/devfs.conf
This file.
.It Pa /etc/rc.d/devfs
Applies it at boot.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Give the console terminal to group
.Li tty
with write permission for the group, and give it a second name:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
own	ttyv0	root:tty
perm	ttyv0	0620
link	ttyv0	vt0
.Ed
.Pp
Let only group
.Li user
use the framebuffers:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
own	fb*	root:user
perm	fb*	0660
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr devfs 4 ,
.Xr rc 8
.Sh HISTORY
The format is
.Fx Ns 's .
